# The upstream this deployment was driven against and verified on. One line per
# step: the name of its foundry profile, then a hash over what solc was fed —
# every .sol file in that step's import closure by content, and the settings it
# compiled them under.
#
# lib/standard and lib/liquid are symlinks to checkouts. A tag would pin the
# checkout and not the symlink, and a working tree has no tag at all, so what
# gets recorded here is what actually determines the bytecode. deploy.sh
# recomputes it and stops before broadcasting anything if the two disagree.
#
# Source alone was the whole preimage once, and it passed a build that was
# nothing like the pinned one: FOUNDRY_OPTIMIZER=false leaves every file
# byte-identical, grows the tokens bytecode 1.85x, and the pin still read green.
# The preimage is now solc's own record of what it was handed — compiler version,
# the whole settings block, source hashes — dropping only the derived half of the
# metadata, since abi and docs follow from sources that are already hashed.
# Excluding that one key beats naming the keys to keep: a setting solc adds later
# is covered the day it lands instead of silently missing.
#
# compilationTarget and libraries read like noise and are not. compilationTarget
# names the file and contract compiled, which deploy.sh fixes by argument, so it
# cannot churn — and compiling a different contract out of the same closure is a
# different deployment. libraries stays empty until a library is linked, and a
# linked address is bytecode.
#
# Moving a line means the deployed contracts change. Exercise the markets against
# the new upstream — deposit, borrow, repay, withdraw — before writing it down.

